[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887050468","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120968#issuecomment-4887050468","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120968","id":4887050468,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0p45A","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T17:56:47Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T17:56:47Z","body":"Nice change. We attempted to fix this a few years ago (before having Grisu2 available) using stb_sprintf and found it provided much worse precision overall. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/96924\r\n\r\nFor the W4 ports, we went with a solution like this (but since it was before Grisu2 was available we used a different third party library). \r\n\r\nOut of curiosity, have you evaluated the difference that Grisu2 makes in this case? Obviously any change will be enough to change the hash signature and break the cache, but I'd be interested to know how much precision gain/loss to expect as well so we can keep an eye on whether it causes any unintended side effects. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887050468/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887175467","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120968#issuecomment-4887175467","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120968","id":4887175467,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0xhKw","user":{"login":"insanepure","id":5879212,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NzkyMTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5879212?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure","html_url":"https://github.com/insanepure","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T18:41:01Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T18:41:01Z","body":"I did not do a precision benchmark on this, but I don't think it is necessary due to the way Grisu2 works.\r\nrtos() has fixed 14 decimals, and here the trailing digits could be different between platforms.\r\n\r\nWith Grisu2, you get the shortest decimal that round trips back to the exact same float.\r\n\r\nSay, in the shader compiler, we have a float constant of 0.1 which will be emitted as a vec4(0.10000000149012,...) via rtos(). where the trailing digits might end up differently.\r\nWith Grisu2, the same constant will be vec4(0.1,...). It will save what is input, not do any rounding or floating imprecision, as Grisu2 is using Integer algorithmics.\r\n\r\nSo there is no loss here, precision for the shader compiler should always be right.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887175467/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887185209","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120968#issuecomment-4887185209","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120968","id":4887185209,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0yHOQ","user":{"login":"insanepure","id":5879212,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NzkyMTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5879212?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure","html_url":"https://github.com/insanepure","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T18:44:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T18:44:25Z","body":"For details see #98750 , which explains Grisu2 quite well.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887185209/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887262025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120968#issuecomment-4887262025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120968","id":4887262025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI02zSQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T19:08:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T19:08:11Z","body":"> For details see #98750 , which explains Grisu2 quite well.\r\n\r\nYou might have missed my comments in there as well as many other comments. There are many cases that Grisu2 handled worse than our existing method that required in-place workarounds. \r\n\r\nMy question above is more about switching from rtos to grisu2, which is not something that was contemplated in #98750","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887262025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887335545","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120968#issuecomment-4887335545","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120968","id":4887335545,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI07SeQ","user":{"login":"insanepure","id":5879212,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NzkyMTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5879212?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure","html_url":"https://github.com/insanepure","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T19:33:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T19:33:06Z","body":"I've read your comments and just double checked others, but I've not found any related to cases where Grisu2 is handling cases that are worse. If you can link me to cases I can evaluate whether that applies here or how it compares.\r\n\r\nI am aware that the num_scientific contains a hack for double, but this here is for float values only, so that should not apply.\r\n\r\nI can also do some example outputs and comparison of using rtos vs grisu2 if that helps.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887335545/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4889863202","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120968#issuecomment-4889863202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120968","id":4889863202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI3VkIg","user":{"login":"Kimau","id":905911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTkxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/905911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau","html_url":"https://github.com/Kimau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T06:44:44Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T06:44:44Z","body":"Good catch I should have found that earlier. Too used to consoles being deterministic and forgot we are baking on host.\r\nWe should likely run a compare against json2 lib to check for variance but nice change.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4889863202/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4995063808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120968#issuecomment-4995063808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120968","id":4995063808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKbqgAA","user":{"login":"insanepure","id":5879212,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NzkyMTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5879212?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure","html_url":"https://github.com/insanepure","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/insanepure/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-16T18:02:39Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T18:06:34Z","body":"I ran a comparison of both paths to check this. I format the float with rtos vs num_scientific, parse it back with strtof and compare the bits.\r\n\r\nFor grisu2 I wrote a small test that iterates over all finite float values (about 2.1 billion, took around 7 minutes 😅). Every value parsed back to the exact same float. This is basically the guarantee of the algorithm (shortest string that round trips to the same float). Thats also the difference to stb in #96924.\r\n\r\nThe old rtos path is exact for typical constants like 0.5 or 3.14 but 14 decimals is not enough for small values. Below ~1e-7 it gets inexact and below ~5e-15 everything just becomes 0.0. So a `const float EPS = 1e-20;` in a shader currently compiles as 0.0.\r\n\r\nSome examples:\r\n\r\n| literal | rtos | num_scientific |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `0.1` | `0.10000000149012` | `0.1` |\r\n| `1e-05` | `0.00000999999975` | `1e-05` |\r\n| `1e-20` | `0.0` | `1e-20` |\r\n| `3.4e38` | `339999995214436424907732413799364296704.0` | `3.4e+38` |\r\n\r\nSo overall its just a precision gain. I found no case where the new path is worse. The double hack from #98750 also doesnt apply here since this uses the float overload.\r\n\r\nThe test program is pretty simple if anyone wants to reproduce the results.\r\n\r\nAs a side note its also around 4x faster than the snprintf path, not that it matters much at shader compile time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4995063808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5005821346","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120968#issuecomment-5005821346","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120968","id":5005821346,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKl7Fog","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-17T17:33:16Z","updated_at":"2026-07-17T17:33:16Z","body":"Thanks! Congratulations on your first merged contribution! 🎉 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5005821346/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]